      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/hardcoded-credentials-and-secrets",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Hardcoded credentials and secrets — Ruled out: Repository current source/config and 9-commit git history\n\nThe flagged RESEND_API_KEY exists only in ignored/untracked operator .env and server deployment .next/standalone/.env; src/lib/email/contact-email.ts:44 reads it only in server API call chain, next.config.ts has no env export, and route.ts:451 returns a fixed generic error rather than exception content. Exact in-memory comparison found no key across 73 source files, 26 public files, 194 production/dev client artifacts, or 252 reachable Git objects; ready local GET /api/health succeeded while /.env, /%2eenv, /.env.local, standalone/static aliases, and source URL all returned 404 without key bytes. No external provider call or credential-validity check was made; remote deployment configuration is not assessed."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Repository current source/config and 9-commit git history"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Hardcoded credentials and secrets",
              "surface": "Repository current source/config and 9-commit git history",
              "recorded_by": "Local Credential Exposure Validator",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/html-injection-semgrep-replaceall-escaping-audit",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "HTML injection / Semgrep replaceAll escaping audit — Ruled out: src/lib/email/contact-email.ts:23-29 HTML email templates\n\nAll attacker-derived strings interpolated into email HTML are passed through escapeHtml, which encodes &, <, >, double quote and apostrophe before text-node insertion; templates contain no attacker-controlled raw HTML, URL attributes, CSS or JavaScript contexts. The four Semgrep matches are chained replaceAll audit warnings for this same context-appropriate control, not bypass evidence."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/lib/email/contact-email.ts:23-29 HTML email templates"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "HTML injection / Semgrep replaceAll escaping audit",
              "surface": "src/lib/email/contact-email.ts:23-29 HTML email templates",
              "recorded_by": "Source Architecture Mapper",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/path-traversal-semgrep-path-join-audit",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Path traversal / Semgrep path.join audit — Ruled out: src/lib/files/al-private-storage.ts:40-61\n\nThe write destination is formed from crypto.randomUUID() plus path.extname(file.name).toLowerCase().slice(0,10), not the original filename; extname extracts an extension without filesystem separators, and the UUID prevents a dot-segment basename. This is the only destination construction before fs.writeFile in the helper. No current callers were found, but that absence is not the basis of closure."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/lib/files/al-private-storage.ts:40-61"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Path traversal / Semgrep path.join audit",
              "surface": "src/lib/files/al-private-storage.ts:40-61",
              "recorded_by": "Source Architecture Mapper",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/authentication-jwt-idor",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "kind": "notApplicable",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Authentication / JWT / IDOR — Not applicable: POST /api/contact authentication and object model\n\nPublic inquiry endpoint has no authentication/session/JWT, persisted user object, tenant, or user-selected private record. Handler constructs explicit contact fields and sends email; it cannot cross account/object boundaries that do not exist."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
